        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_Flat",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Salt Flat sits at 3,730 feet near the Guadalupe Mountains, preserving early Texas settlement history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/salt-flat-texas-ghost-town/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Salt Flat’s historic stone building served travelers on the Butterfield Trail and remains a symbol of Texas frontier life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/salt-flat-texas-ghost-town/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Salt Flat’s name reflects ancient salt deposits that sparked territorial conflicts long before its founding.",
